      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our circle is centered at $(1,1)$ and has a radius of $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}={4}^{2}\\,\u27f9\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=16.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(16) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-1)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y-1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)+2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x-1}{y-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
